lls show him tied or ahead, while markets price him near 68%. The state's Republican lean and Husted's incumbency keep this from being Likely D, but the weight of recent evidence favors the Democrat.", "watch": "A late shift among Republican-leaning voters consolidating behind Husted, or Libertarian votes siphoning from him less than expected, could close the polling gap.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Husted (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's special Senate race pits appointed Republican incumbent Jon Husted against former Senator Sherrod Brown in one of the cycle's most competitive contests. Recent polls from mid-to-late October uniformly show Brown ahead by about three to five points, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters, though one Rasmussen poll had Husted up two. Averages across major trackers put Brown up roughly three points.\n\nExpert raters split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets price Brown's chances near two-thirds. Brown has raised far more money than Husted, but outside groups have spent heavily against him. The state's five-point Republican lean and Husted's incumbency temper the polling edge, leaving the race rated Lean D with meaningful uncertainty in the final days.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7221, "margin": 2.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7246, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6986, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6393, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6851, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7568, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7432, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7463, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7417, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7438, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7437, "margin": 3.0}